     "text": "Printed by: ROI_61 11/09/2026\nCONFIDENTIAL - Contains PHI\nSchmidt-Martinez Clinic | Dr. Brandon Herman, family medicine\nPatient: Wesley Bridges DOB: 02/29/2000 Sex: M MRN: 519094\n\n---\n\n**PROBLEM LIST:**\n\n- GERD [controlled] onset 05/2026\n- Gout [controlled] onset 08/2024\n- Seasonal Allergy [controlled] onset 12/2019\n\n---\n\n**MEDICATIONS:**\n\n- Omeprazole 20 mg\n- Famotidine 20 mg\n- Colchicine 0.6 mg\n- Allopurinol 300 mg\n- Cetirizine 10 mg\n- Fluticasone nasal 50 mcg\n\n---\n\n**ENCOUNTERS:**\n\n---\n\n**06/23/2026 - Office Visit**\n\n**S:** Patient presents for follow-up on seasonal allergy. Reports no significant change in symptoms. No new complaints.\n\n**O:** \n- BP: 144/83 mmHg\n- Weight: 225 lb\n- Physical Exam: \n - HEENT: Normocephalic, atraumatic. Nasal mucosa without erythema or edema. Throat without erythema or exudate.\n - Cardiovascular: Regular rate and rhythm, no murmurs, rubs, or gallops.\n - Respiratory: Clear to auscultation bilaterally, no wheezing, rales, or rhonchi.\n - Abdomen: Soft, non-tender, no hepatosplenomegaly.\n\n**A:** Seasonal allergy - unchanged.\n\n**P:** Continue current treatment with cetirizine and fluticasone. Return clinic in 3-6 months for re-evaluation.\n\n---\n\n**06/18/2025 - Office Visit**\n\n**S:** Patient presents for follow-up on gout. Reports no recent flare-ups. No new complaints.\n\n**O:** \n- BP: 135/81 mmHg\n- Weight: 223 lb\n- Physical Exam: \n - HEENT: Normocephalic, atraumatic.\n - Cardiovascular: Regular rate and rhythm.\n - Musculoskeletal: No signs of inflammation or tenderness in joints.\n - Abdomen: Soft, non-tender.\n\n**A:** Gout - unchanged.\n\n**P:** Continue current treatment with colchicine and allopurinol. Return to clinic in 3-6 months for re-evaluation.\n\n---\n\n**06/13/2024 - Office Visit**\n\n**S:** Patient presents for follow-up on seasonal allergy. Reports typical seasonal symptoms, well-controlled with current medications. No new complaints.\n\n**O:** \n- BP: 13